assertion  XCU.sh-lists.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3/equal precedence
class      required
says       && and || have equal precedence and group from the left.
test       t/001-and-or-assoc.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-lists.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.3
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.4
class      required
says       The status of an AND or OR list is the status of the last command
           that was executed.
test       t/002-and-or-status.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-lists.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.2
class      required
says       Lists separated by ; or newline run one after the other, and the
           status is that of the last one run.
test       t/003-sequential.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-lists.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.3
class      required
says       The commands of an AND or OR list are expanded only when they are
           executed.
test       t/004-expand-only-executed.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-lists.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.1
class      required
says       A command ended with & runs in the background: the shell goes on
           without waiting for it, and wait can collect it later.
test       t/005-async-no-wait.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-lists.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.1/The exit status of an asynchronous AND-OR list shall be zero
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.1/The exit status of the subshell
class      required
says       The status of an asynchronous list as seen when the shell goes on
           is zero; its real status is available through wait on $!.
test       t/006-async-status.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-lists.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.1/If, and only if, job control is disabled
class      required
says       When job control is off, an asynchronous list gets /dev/null as
           standard input unless it redirects it.
test       t/007-async-stdin.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-lists.008
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.3.1
class      required
says       Several asynchronous lists in one line all run; wait with no
           operand waits for all of them.
test       t/008-async-several.sh
